!configs/
# Removed 2026-09-06: negations for analytics_report.json, analytics_prev.json,
# intelligence_report.json and title_ab.json. They were added 2026-07-05 for a
# real bug — the blanket *.json above stopped the analytics workflow committing
# its reports — but THERE IS NO ANALYTICS WORKFLOW IN THIS REPO. All four files
# are untracked, absent, and written by nothing here; they were the Money Sorted
# workflow's data bus. Quizora dropped the same four on 2026-08-02.
#
# The one surviving reader, quality_scorer._load_channel_learnings(), is guarded
# and returns {} — it has never fired. **If an analytics workflow is ever added
# to this repo, restore these four negations first**, or the blanket *.json will
# swallow its output and reproduce the 2026-07-05 bug exactly.
!affiliates.json
# Playlist-id cache: must be tracked or every CI run starts cold and the
# get-or-create fallback can mint duplicate playlists (found 2026-07-11).
!playlist_map.json
# Ledgers MUST be tracked or every Actions run picks the same daily topic
# (avoid-last-15 sees an empty history) — found on first Actions run.
!anim_ledger.json
!topic_ledger.json
!compilation_ledger.json
# Same rule as the ledgers above: these are read by the pipeline in CI, so the
# blanket *.json must not swallow them. bg_used.json stops the same Pexels photo
# being reused across videos (repetitious-content risk); question_bank.json is
# the approved question supply.
!bg_used.json
!question_bank.json
.env
github_pat.txt
pexels_api.txt

